{"name":"Rogue Blue","hex":"#4b5764","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rogue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A scoundrel, rascal or unprincipled, deceitful, and unreliable person.","A mischievous scamp."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Vicious and solitary.","Large, destructive and unpredictable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rogue"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rogue (Marvel Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Rogue is a character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics, commonly in association with the X-Men. She first appeared in The Avengers Annual #10 (1981). In the Marvel Universe, Rogue is depicted as a mutant, a subspecies of humans born with an \"X-gene\" that grants superhuman abilities. She is capable of absorbing the life force, attributes, memories, and superpowers of anyone through physical touch. The character is initially portrayed as a reluctant supervillain, but she soon joins the X-Men as a superhero and has since endured as one of its most prominent members."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d3/Excalibur_2019_-18.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rogue_(Marvel_Comics)","wikidata":"Q838097"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/95/Rogue_%28Marvel_Comics%29.png/250px-Rogue_%28Marvel_Comics%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/95/Rogue_%28Marvel_Comics%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/95/Rogue_%28Marvel_Comics%29.png/250px-Rogue_%28Marvel_Comics%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"For many years, Rogue used a pair of gloves to regulate her uncontrollable mutant absorption abilities","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARogue_(Marvel_Comics).png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Anna_Paquin_Rogue.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Anna_Paquin_Rogue.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Anna Paquin as Rogue in a promotional poster for X-Men: Days of Future Past - The Rogue Cut (2015)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnna_Paquin_Rogue.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/20